<title>RUSSIA: Rouble tracks lower c.bank rates on T-bill supply.</title>
<headline>Rouble tracks lower c.bank rates on T-bill supply.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased on Friday following a slightly quicker decline of the central bank's rates and dealers said the government bond market still seemed the main source of funds.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Dec 20 midday  Dec 20 early   Dec 19 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,552-53	 5,552-54	 5,545-46</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,552-54	 5,549-50	 5,549-50</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)    5-10	    10-15	     5-10</p>
<p>			   Dec 20				Dec 19</p>
<p> central bank	  5,545/55			    5,541/51</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,545				 5,542</p>
<p>&quot;Today the central bank has raised its (dollar) rates a little more than usual (one to three points) and it could bring banks to buy dollars more actively,&quot; a Stolichny Bank dealer said.</p>
<p>Another dealer said some funds had left the Treasury bill market and thet was enough to make the rouble edge down.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
